Cell[TextData[{
 "Play with the animation controls on the eccentricity, slowing it down by 12 \
clicks or so to watch the change from death-spiral to stable florets around \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"ecc", "=", "0.69"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a1131eef-ed80-4402-afda-81c4dfbb57cb"],
 ". "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.977845035410708*^9, 3.977845082208993*^9}, {
  3.977845123829846*^9, 
  3.97784512975949*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b1c0eebc-38e6-4c70-8bc2-\
5bf3d2496369"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Conclusion", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9775359255386477`*^9, 
  3.977535927492813*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"44078a61-e046-484d-88fb-\
bf9ffa1a9329"],

Cell["\<\
In previous posts on the \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] calculus, we \
focused on building the machinery: defining tensors, algebraic structures, \
and prototyping a compiler. In this post, we step back from just building the \
tool and use it for astrophysical science. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.977870710769527*^9, {3.977871757225184*^9, 3.977871857921623*^9}, {
   3.977872202764914*^9, 3.977872206642281*^9}, {3.977872430055544*^9, 
   3.977872465327394*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c497708a-95bf-463f-b12e-\
7bb8a4b99aaf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The best part of this experiment is what we ",
 StyleBox["didn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " have to do. To simulate the extreme environment of a Schwarzschild black \
hole, where space-time curves, time slows, and orbits precess, we did not \
write new physics code. We simply fed the Schwarzschild metric into our \
existing \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] compiler, cranked out the \
Christoffel symbols, and let the standard geodesic equation do the rest."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.977870710769527*^9, {3.977871757225184*^9, 
   3.977871962711142*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"91226afa-abb3-410c-ac03-\
a084759befd3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In the Smoke Test, we metaphorically reproduce the famous Precession of the \
Perihelion of Mercury around the Sun, just with a much heavier \
orbit-producing black hole. In the ",
 StyleBox["Manipulate", "Input"],
 " demonstration, we can push parameters to probe the Innermost Stable \
Circular Orbit (ISCO) and visually confirm our test star vanishes from the \
Universe at the event horizon."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.977870710769527*^9, {3.977871757225184*^9, 3.977872214627316*^9}, {
   3.978992092688534*^9, 
   3.978992101681294*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f17948d7-06b2-4c87-b74d-\
004b37b6c256"],

Cell["\<\
This exercise confirms that \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] is solid, so \
far. It can serve as a foundation for exploring more complex geometries such \
as the Kerr metric, and ventured in future posts into quantum gauge theories.\
\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.977870710769527*^9, {3.977871757225184*^9, 
   3.977872369280204*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0cca20ba-b9d4-4656-b677-\
e6b0db47005d"],

Cell["\<\
For now, please enjoy the Interactive Lab. Crash some stars, search for \
resonances in precession, and explore the fearsome math of general relativity.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.977870710769527*^9, {3.977871757225184*^9, 
   3.977872420805355*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e6785368-9b01-4f96-b600-\
072a44d1545e"]
}, Open  ]],

